1
00:01:26,353 --> 00:01:29,958
Any minute now. You see,
you can't rush it, baby girl.

2
00:01:29,991 --> 00:01:32,994
The secret to fishing
is patience.

3
00:01:33,027 --> 00:01:35,395
It's been
five hours, Dad.

4
00:01:35,429 --> 00:01:37,932
How much more patience
do we need?

5
00:01:37,966 --> 00:01:40,935
Don't ask me.
Ask the fish.

6
00:01:42,102 --> 00:01:44,204
What's up, guys?
It's your boy, Dustin.

7
00:01:44,237 --> 00:01:46,173
I'm out on the boat,
and once again,

8
00:01:46,206 --> 00:01:48,843
my dad can't catch
any fish.

9
00:01:48,876 --> 00:01:50,545
Hey! I heard that.

10
00:01:50,578 --> 00:01:53,615
Don't worry, sweetheart,
I caught these this morning.

11
00:01:53,648 --> 00:01:55,282
At the grocery store.

12
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:58,820
Mom, I'm live!
So embarrassing!

13
00:02:07,962 --> 00:02:10,531
Mr. Fluffy Butt, no!

14
00:02:10,565 --> 00:02:11,532
Bad kitty!

15
00:02:13,901 --> 00:02:15,168
Whoa.

16
00:02:15,202 --> 00:02:16,203
Uh... Dad?

17
00:02:16,236 --> 00:02:17,237
Dad!

18
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:20,173
Shh! Quiet.
You'll scare the fishies.

19
00:02:20,207 --> 00:02:22,376
The boat's on fire!

20
00:02:31,886 --> 00:02:34,388
Down! Ready... set.

21
00:02:34,789 --> 00:02:35,690
Ruff!

22
00:02:36,858 --> 00:02:38,826
Skye! Skye, I'm open!

23
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,360
Marshall, go long!

24
00:02:41,829 --> 00:02:44,431
I got it. I got it. I-- Whoa!

25
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:48,636
Oof!

26
00:02:48,670 --> 00:02:50,404
Marshall!

27
00:02:50,437 --> 00:02:52,205
I'm okay!

28
00:02:52,239 --> 00:02:54,809
Pass is incomplete.
Flag on the play.

29
00:02:54,842 --> 00:02:56,544
Ten yards for clumsiness.

30
00:03:01,115 --> 00:03:02,984
<i>Mayday, mayday! S.O.S.!</i>

31
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,318
<i>Our cat set our boat on fire!</i>

32
00:03:05,352 --> 00:03:06,688
This is the PAW Patrol.

33
00:03:06,721 --> 00:03:09,423
S.O.S. received.
We're on our way.

34
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:16,931
Come on, pups.
Ryder needs us.

35
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:24,371
That was my first touchdown!
It's still gonna count, right?

36
00:03:24,939 --> 00:03:26,373
Hey, wait up!

37
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:28,375
<i>All right, pups.</i>

38
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:30,078
<i>We've got</i>
<i>a five-alarm boat fire</i>

39
00:03:30,111 --> 00:03:31,846
<i>and there are people onboard.</i>

40
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:36,283
<i>Zuma, you are go for launch.</i>

41
00:03:36,316 --> 00:03:37,885
Aye-aye, Ryder, sir!

42
00:03:48,629 --> 00:03:51,699
<i>Skye, let's get eyes</i>
<i>on that boat ASAP.</i>

43
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:52,967
I'm on it.

44
00:03:56,204 --> 00:03:59,574
Marshall, Chase, Rubble,
let's fight that fire.

45
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:05,580
Hoses on!

46
00:04:08,983 --> 00:04:10,785
Help! Up here!
Help!

47
00:04:10,818 --> 00:04:12,153
We're up here!

48
00:04:12,186 --> 00:04:15,489
My name's Zuma
and I'll be your rescue pup.

49
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,327
All right!
Oh, thank goodness.

50
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:23,396
It's time for you dudes
to ride the slide.

51
00:04:24,699 --> 00:04:26,134
Whoo-hoo!

52
00:04:26,167 --> 00:04:27,502
Whoa!

53
00:04:28,202 --> 00:04:29,537
Oh!

54
00:04:31,906 --> 00:04:32,907
Whoo!

55
00:04:34,142 --> 00:04:36,577
<i>All right, pups,</i>
<i>it's showtime!</i>

56
00:04:40,148 --> 00:04:42,550
Man, this video is fire!

57
00:04:42,583 --> 00:04:45,720
Dustin, get off your phone
and evacuate.

58
00:04:45,753 --> 00:04:48,656
Oh. Gotta go.
Like and subscribe.

59
00:04:48,689 --> 00:04:50,792
Hup! Whoo-hoo!

60
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,326
That's everyone.

61
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,662
Whoo-hoo!

62
00:04:54,695 --> 00:04:56,664
<i>Nice work, Zuma.</i>

63
00:04:56,697 --> 00:04:59,267
The cat!
Hey, where's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

64
00:04:59,299 --> 00:05:01,903
He must still be onboard.

65
00:05:01,936 --> 00:05:04,972
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

66
00:05:05,006 --> 00:05:07,241
Pups, we've got a cat onboard.

67
00:05:07,275 --> 00:05:09,243
It's always a cat.

68
00:05:09,277 --> 00:05:11,378
Stuck in a tree,
stuck in a boat...

69
00:05:11,411 --> 00:05:13,380
Don't worry. I'm on it.

70
00:05:27,862 --> 00:05:31,464
Okay, Marshall.
No clumsiness, no mistakes.

71
00:05:39,406 --> 00:05:43,077
Here, kitty,
kitty, kitty! Hello!

72
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:45,112
Mr. Fluffy Butt!

73
00:05:45,146 --> 00:05:47,882
Kitty, where are you?

74
00:05:57,124 --> 00:06:00,127
Looks like we're gonna have
to do this the hard way.

75
00:06:00,161 --> 00:06:01,562
Fire axes!

76
00:06:08,135 --> 00:06:09,503
I found the kitty.

77
00:06:09,537 --> 00:06:12,940
He's actually pretty cute.
For a cat.

78
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:17,812
<i>Marshall,</i>
<i>your exit is blocked.</i>

79
00:06:17,845 --> 00:06:20,014
<i>You're gonna have to find</i>
<i>another way out.</i>

80
00:06:20,047 --> 00:06:20,982
Copy that.

81
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:27,154
Sorry about this, kitty.

82
00:06:37,198 --> 00:06:38,431
Oh, no!

83
00:06:38,465 --> 00:06:39,901
Come on, man.

84
00:06:39,934 --> 00:06:41,002
Where are they?

85
00:06:41,035 --> 00:06:42,469
No...
Oh, no.

86
00:06:44,906 --> 00:06:46,173
Yeah!

87
00:06:46,207 --> 00:06:48,843
That wasn't so bad,
was it, kitty?

88
00:06:51,444 --> 00:06:54,081
Come to mommy.
Come to mommy.

89
00:06:54,115 --> 00:06:57,518
Oh, my baby. Mwah.

90
00:06:57,551 --> 00:07:00,354
Ugh. Are you sure
that's Mr. Fluffy Butt?

91
00:07:01,822 --> 00:07:03,024
Don't worry.

92
00:07:03,057 --> 00:07:06,060
His butt will fluff up again
as soon as he dries off.

93
00:07:07,628 --> 00:07:11,265
Loop, swoop, and pull.

94
00:07:11,299 --> 00:07:13,868
All right,
the hitch is hooked!

95
00:07:13,901 --> 00:07:14,969
Don't worry, kids.

96
00:07:15,002 --> 00:07:17,505
Captain Turbot is the O.G.
of the high seas.

97
00:07:17,538 --> 00:07:19,640
He'll have us back
to land in no time.

98
00:07:19,674 --> 00:07:21,309
You know it!

99
00:07:21,342 --> 00:07:23,144
Goodbye, Cap'n Turbot!
Goodbye!

100
00:07:23,177 --> 00:07:24,545
Farewell, friends!
Bye!

101
00:07:24,578 --> 00:07:27,014
See you later!
Stay cool,
little doggies!

102
00:07:27,048 --> 00:07:28,549
Bye, Mr. Fluffy Butt!

103
00:07:28,582 --> 00:07:32,086
Nice work, Marshall.
That was a perfect rescue.

104
00:07:32,119 --> 00:07:33,220
What can I say?

105
00:07:33,254 --> 00:07:35,790
Rescue pups
don't make mistakes.

106
00:07:39,794 --> 00:07:42,296
Looks like we're heading
into some weather.

107
00:07:42,330 --> 00:07:43,764
Buckle up, pups.

108
00:07:51,471 --> 00:07:53,941
Whoa!

109
00:07:53,975 --> 00:07:55,676
Whoa!

110
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:57,945
Isn't this fun?

111
00:07:57,979 --> 00:08:01,782
I think
I'm more of a land mammal.

112
00:08:13,127 --> 00:08:14,996
Switch on the fog lights!

113
00:08:15,029 --> 00:08:16,797
Switching on fog lights.

114
00:08:26,374 --> 00:08:27,441
Ryder,

115
00:08:27,475 --> 00:08:29,176
we're drifting off course.

116
00:08:29,210 --> 00:08:32,813
I'm flying blind out here!
The instruments
are going crazy.

117
00:08:32,847 --> 00:08:35,149
That's comforting.

118
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,551
Wait, what is that?

119
00:08:38,052 --> 00:08:39,553
What on earth?

120
00:08:42,089 --> 00:08:44,091
Oh, no. No. No, no, no!

121
00:08:45,126 --> 00:08:46,394
Brace for impact!

122
00:08:51,499 --> 00:08:53,300
Whoa!

123
00:09:08,517 --> 00:09:09,583
Ugh.

124
00:09:11,152 --> 00:09:12,386
Ugh.

125
00:09:24,098 --> 00:09:28,469
This doesn't make any sense.
There's no island on the map.

126
00:09:28,503 --> 00:09:30,805
I guess it's time
to update the map.

127
00:09:31,739 --> 00:09:34,008
So what do
we do now?

128
00:09:34,041 --> 00:09:36,577
We've got
to explore the island.

129
00:09:36,610 --> 00:09:37,711
Marshall's
right.

130
00:09:37,745 --> 00:09:39,680
But if we're going
into that jungle,

131
00:09:39,713 --> 00:09:41,749
we need to suit up
for the job.

132
00:09:43,217 --> 00:09:44,085
<i>All right, pups,</i>

133
00:09:44,118 --> 00:09:46,187
<i>these are</i>
<i>your new survival suits.</i>

134
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:49,490
<i>They've got</i>
<i>everything you need</i>
<i>to stay alive in the jungle.</i>

135
00:09:49,524 --> 00:09:51,292
<i>Protection from the elements.</i>

136
00:09:51,325 --> 00:09:52,660
<i>Safety gear for climbing.</i>

137
00:09:52,693 --> 00:09:54,695
<i>Built-in floatation devices.</i>

138
00:09:54,728 --> 00:09:58,099
<i>Flashlights, compass</i>
<i>and G.P.S.</i>

139
00:09:58,132 --> 00:10:00,367
<i>Whatever this island</i>
<i>throws at us,</i>

140
00:10:00,401 --> 00:10:01,869
<i>we'll be prepared.</i>

141
00:10:05,606 --> 00:10:07,842
Ready for action,
Ryder, sir!

142
00:10:18,986 --> 00:10:21,422
This place
is amazing.

143
00:10:21,455 --> 00:10:23,858
Everything
is so huge.

144
00:10:24,692 --> 00:10:26,193
Let's climb
to the top of that cliff

145
00:10:26,227 --> 00:10:27,728
and get a lay of the land.

146
00:10:42,577 --> 00:10:43,477
Ugh.

147
00:10:43,512 --> 00:10:46,113
Wow. Look at that view!

148
00:10:54,288 --> 00:10:55,557
Dudes.

149
00:10:55,590 --> 00:10:57,191
It's incredible.

150
00:10:57,224 --> 00:11:00,494
And I've got
the best seat
in the house.

151
00:11:00,529 --> 00:11:01,729
Whoa.

152
00:11:09,604 --> 00:11:10,938
I'm okay!

153
00:11:10,971 --> 00:11:13,841
Marshall!

154
00:11:15,976 --> 00:11:17,711
Marshall!

155
00:11:17,745 --> 00:11:20,214
What? I said I'm okay.
It's kind of my thing.

156
00:11:20,247 --> 00:11:22,383
I crash into something,
then I pop back up

157
00:11:22,416 --> 00:11:23,585
and say, "I'm okay!"

158
00:11:23,618 --> 00:11:24,653
People seem to like it.

159
00:11:24,685 --> 00:11:26,655
Marshall, run!

160
00:11:29,624 --> 00:11:32,359
What on earth
is that thing?!

161
00:11:38,499 --> 00:11:40,401
Come on! Go, go, go!

162
00:11:44,972 --> 00:11:46,541
Run!

163
00:11:46,575 --> 00:11:48,742
I am running!

164
00:11:48,776 --> 00:11:52,713
I'm a bulldog, this is as fast
as I can go!

165
00:11:52,746 --> 00:11:54,748
Is that a dinosaur?

166
00:11:54,782 --> 00:11:56,651
I thought those things
were extinct!

167
00:12:08,597 --> 00:12:10,532
Don't eat me! Don't eat me!

168
00:12:10,565 --> 00:12:11,865
Marshall!

169
00:12:34,154 --> 00:12:36,957
Get out of here,
you old cranky pants!

170
00:12:46,834 --> 00:12:48,637
You woke her up, didn't you?

171
00:12:48,670 --> 00:12:50,672
Wha-- W-What?

172
00:12:50,705 --> 00:12:51,972
Don't take it personally.

173
00:12:52,006 --> 00:12:55,376
That Spinosaurus is always
cranky after her nap.

174
00:12:58,245 --> 00:13:00,749
Boy, is it good to see
some other pups!

175
00:13:00,781 --> 00:13:02,617
It's just been me
and the dinosaurs

176
00:13:02,651 --> 00:13:04,753
for the last
two and a half years.

177
00:13:07,388 --> 00:13:10,491
Oh, how rude of me! I'm Rex.

178
00:13:10,525 --> 00:13:12,426
And this is Timmy the T-Rex.

179
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:18,132
Timmy is t-t-terrifying.

180
00:13:18,165 --> 00:13:19,701
No, he's not.

181
00:13:19,734 --> 00:13:21,268
You're not terrifying.

182
00:13:21,302 --> 00:13:24,171
You're a good boy,
aren't you, buddy?

183
00:13:24,204 --> 00:13:26,807
Yeah, you're a good boy.

184
00:13:32,179 --> 00:13:34,848
H-How are there
dinosaurs here?

185
00:13:34,882 --> 00:13:37,985
How-- How are you here?
What's going on?

186
00:13:38,018 --> 00:13:40,187
I'm sure you got
a lot of questions.

187
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,855
Why don't you let me
show you around,

188
00:13:41,889 --> 00:13:45,025
and I'll do my best
to answer as many as I can.

189
00:13:49,063 --> 00:13:50,765
I've been stranded
on this island

190
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:53,133
since I fell overboard
during a storm.

191
00:13:53,167 --> 00:13:55,135
The first time
I saw a dinosaur,

192
00:13:55,169 --> 00:13:57,271
I almost jumped out of my fur.

193
00:13:57,304 --> 00:13:59,139
But they're actually
really friendly

194
00:13:59,173 --> 00:14:00,508
when you get to know them.

195
00:14:03,877 --> 00:14:05,513
Come on, follow me.

196
00:14:07,582 --> 00:14:08,449
Ha!

197
00:14:13,822 --> 00:14:15,356
Whoa!

198
00:14:15,389 --> 00:14:17,124
He is so cool.

199
00:14:17,157 --> 00:14:20,160
The pup's got moves,
no doubt about it.

200
00:14:24,799 --> 00:14:27,101
Whoa--

201
00:14:27,134 --> 00:14:30,170
Wait, whoa, whoa--
Whoa! Whoa, whoa, whoa!

202
00:14:31,606 --> 00:14:33,641
Marshall!

203
00:14:33,675 --> 00:14:35,409
Sorry about that.

204
00:14:35,442 --> 00:14:38,912
In case you haven't guessed,
I'm the clumsy pup.

205
00:14:38,946 --> 00:14:40,615
It's all good.
Keep trying.

206
00:14:40,648 --> 00:14:44,118
Everybody makes mistakes
when they're learning
something new.

207
00:14:44,853 --> 00:14:46,253
Whoa. Look!

208
00:14:52,926 --> 00:14:54,962
Oh! Hello.

209
00:14:54,995 --> 00:14:56,497
Ah!

210
00:14:56,531 --> 00:14:58,833
Oh-- Uh...

211
00:15:01,235 --> 00:15:03,303
They're just shy.

212
00:15:03,337 --> 00:15:05,239
They'll get used
to you soon enough.

213
00:15:05,807 --> 00:15:07,575
Okay, this is me.

214
00:15:18,986 --> 00:15:22,590
Whoa. Rex,
you built all this?

215
00:15:22,624 --> 00:15:26,861
Yep. It's taken me
two years, a hundred
and forty-seven days,

216
00:15:26,895 --> 00:15:28,663
and I'm almost done.

217
00:15:43,778 --> 00:15:46,614
Whoa! Whoa.

218
00:15:51,753 --> 00:15:53,187
All aboard.

219
00:15:53,621 --> 00:15:54,488
Hup.

220
00:15:57,124 --> 00:15:59,126
Oh! Whoa--
Whoa, whoa.

221
00:16:00,628 --> 00:16:02,062
Whoa!

222
00:16:04,532 --> 00:16:06,066
Whoo!

223
00:16:28,823 --> 00:16:30,491
Thanks for the lift, Nellie!

224
00:16:34,896 --> 00:16:36,798
Hey!

225
00:16:40,635 --> 00:16:43,671
It was always my dream
to build my own treehouse.

226
00:16:43,705 --> 00:16:47,509
When I got stranded out here,
I finally got the chance.

227
00:16:49,511 --> 00:16:51,011
Whoa!

228
00:16:51,513 --> 00:16:53,480
This is incredible!

229
00:16:53,515 --> 00:16:56,818
It's all made
out of stuff I found
on the island.

230
00:16:56,851 --> 00:16:58,753
It's amazing how much nature
will give you

231
00:16:58,786 --> 00:17:00,354
if you know where to look.

232
00:17:01,255 --> 00:17:03,791
Welcome to my home sweet home.

233
00:17:03,825 --> 00:17:05,660
It doesn't have
air conditioning,

234
00:17:05,693 --> 00:17:07,896
a big screen TV or Wi-Fi...

235
00:17:09,296 --> 00:17:10,765
...but it does the trick.

236
00:17:11,331 --> 00:17:12,700
Wow!

237
00:17:12,734 --> 00:17:16,905
Dude, this is the coolest
treehouse in the world!

238
00:17:16,938 --> 00:17:20,173
It's glamping. I could
totally get behind this.

239
00:17:20,207 --> 00:17:22,577
Plus, being up this high
must give you some privacy

240
00:17:22,610 --> 00:17:23,811
from all the dinosaurs.

241
00:17:23,845 --> 00:17:25,212
Ah!

242
00:17:25,947 --> 00:17:27,515
Or maybe not.

243
00:17:31,019 --> 00:17:33,420
If you really want to see
Dino Island,

244
00:17:33,453 --> 00:17:35,590
there's only one way
to do it.

245
00:17:37,224 --> 00:17:40,028
Do you want to go
for a ride?

246
00:17:42,129 --> 00:17:44,599
<i>♪ Something about you</i>
<i>Got me</i>

247
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:47,367
<i>♪ Like lightning struck</i>

248
00:17:47,401 --> 00:17:48,870
<i>♪ My body</i>

249
00:17:48,903 --> 00:17:50,705
<i>♪ Tell the room</i>
<i>Get out the way</i>

250
00:17:50,738 --> 00:17:51,773
Yeah!

251
00:17:51,806 --> 00:17:52,907
<i>♪ We are made of broken pieces</i>

252
00:17:52,941 --> 00:17:55,009
<i>♪ But that's how</i>
<i>The love gets in</i>

253
00:17:55,043 --> 00:17:57,277
Whoo-hoo!

254
00:17:57,311 --> 00:17:59,112
<i>♪ You're under my skin</i>

255
00:17:59,146 --> 00:18:01,716
Check it out! Triceratops!

256
00:18:03,150 --> 00:18:05,653
<i>♪ Ooh, if you're feeling</i>
<i>The love go deeper</i>

257
00:18:05,687 --> 00:18:07,722
<i>♪ And deeper, come down</i>
Whoo-hoo!

258
00:18:07,755 --> 00:18:10,024
